{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Mighty one.</b> Who has strength." "<b>And a man of war.</b> Who is practiced." "<b>Judge.</b> Who is asked to instruct us in the straight path of religion; and likewise the prophet, also the diviner, in the wisdom of the constellations." "<b>Elder.</b> Who has tested the affairs of the world."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:15.366805754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}